Design notes:

- P1 traffic: every frame is copied to P3. Intra-segment IPv4 (10.0.2.0/24 to 10.0.2.0/24) and ARP also go to P2. All other P1 traffic goes to P3 only.
- P3 traffic: all of it returns to P1 only.
- P2 traffic: IPv4 to the segment (dst 10.0.2.0/24) and ARP go to P1. Everything else is dropped by the table-miss default.
- Priorities: the specific P1 rules sit above the catch-all P1 rule, because rules are not additive and the highest matching one wins.

